A value that is not valid Jinja fails with exit 2, naming the broken value on stderr, and
writes nothing.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
status: backlog
---
# My Plan

- [ ] 3 SP: Task one
- [ ] 2 SP: Task two
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md value="{{ macro( }}"
-- exit --
2
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
error: value '{{ macro( }}': TemplateSyntaxError: unexpected '}', expected ')'
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
status: backlog
---
# My Plan

- [ ] 3 SP: Task one
- [ ] 2 SP: Task two
